        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: remove browser and codex dead exports",
        "body": "Related: #105595\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nRemoves 555 unused production exports from the browser and Codex plugins so the shrink-only dead-export ratchet reflects code that is actually reachable in production.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBrowser Playwright helpers now use one canonical export path instead of duplicate re-export chains. Other dead plugin exports and tests that existed only to cover them were deleted; Codex protocol-shaped surfaces were checked against the sibling Codex source, while plugin entry barrels and canonical protocol namespaces remain intact.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Maintainers get a smaller plugin surface and a dead-export baseline reduced from 5,962 to 5,404 entries.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` regenerated the baseline; `pnpm deadcode:exports` passes with zero browser or Codex entries.\n- Browser suite: 138 files, 1,796 passed, 1 skipped; focused proxy/chrome reruns: 56 passed.\n- Codex non-live shards: 2,428 passed; post-cleanup focused rerun: 767 passed.\n- `pnpm check:test-types`: core, extensions, and root test typechecks passed.\n- `pnpm check:changed`: format, SDK baseline, package guards, all typechecks, and core lint passed; the sole extension-lint finding was four stale test imports, then focused extension lint and 35-test rerun passed.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview split across the large change and both follow-up fixes: no remaining actionable findings.\n",
